meta {
  name: Update bill
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/bills/{{billId}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "description": "Updated via Bruno",
    "dueDate": "2026-06-15T00:00:00.000Z"
  }
}

docs {
  Admin only. PATCH on a bill in PAID/REJECTED/ARCHIVED returns
  409 BILL_NOT_EDITABLE with `details.status`. Sending `null` on
  required-non-null fields (amount/currency/invoiceDate/dueDate)
  returns 400 VALIDATION_ERROR.

  Post-payment field lock: once a non-cancelled Payment row exists for
  the bill, the financial fields are frozen because editing them would
  drift from the Payment row. Attempting `amount`, `currency`, or
  `paymentMethod` returns
      409 BILL_FIELD_LOCKED_POST_PAYMENT
      details: { lockedFields: [...], paymentStatus }
  `description`, `dueDate`, and `invoiceDate` stay editable — memo /
  tracking / typo-correction don't affect the payment.

  Pre-approve, `paymentMethod` is consulted at approve time only. Send
  a method value to override the vendor default, or `null` to clear:
      "paymentMethod": "WIRE"
      "paymentMethod": null
}
